WEBVTT

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:05.980
<i>Guerrilla... Guerrilla...</i>

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.500
<i>Guerrilla...</i>

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.190
Tsubasa-sama.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.650
Sensei is producing Lyric?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.490
Guerrilla... Guerrilla...

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.490
Yes. He began a short while ago.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.280
Could they be lyrics for a new song?

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.740
<i>Guerrilla... Guerrilla...</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.830
<i>Gross-out... Funny faces...</i>

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.330
<i>Bungee...</i>

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.200
"Bungee"...

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.720
Chieri's amazing!

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.100
Ever since the trial was broadcast, her popularity has exploded.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.060
She's got more solo work, too.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.600
This must be what they call a "power push".

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.980
With all this work as of late, she's
been too busy to perform in concerts.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.690
We're falling behind.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.980
Yeah.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.730
With this much exposure, it will
probably affect the General Elections.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:08.540
<i>This broadcast might have
secured her spot in the Elections.</i>

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.550
The General Elections, huh?

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.280
And I'd <i>just</i> managed to forget about it!

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.220
Gosh! I'm sick of this!

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.490
The votes are already being collected.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.180
CDs that come with ballots are on sale.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:29.020
Download numbers are
also showing a dramatic rise.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.410
It's really happening.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.000
The General Elections...

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:41.180
A future in which mankind has moved to
space and entertainment has been banned.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:46.440
One idol group continues to put on illegal concerts: AKB0048.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.230
The young girls put their lives on the line to sing with radiance.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.810
A wind that heeds no master now blows.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.970
A guerrilla channel?

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.490
As our next initiative following the revival of the General Elections,

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:31.940
we're starting a 00-exclusive guerrilla channel to broadcast TV shows.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.230
And you want us to appear on it?

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.260
That's right.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:41.670
But what will we be doing on those TV shows?

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.780
Huh? You mean you don't know?

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.910
TV on Lancastar was only ever news or weather.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.760
You gotta be kidding!

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:53.130
Is it because entertainment
was banned there for so long?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.140
Makoto-san's home planet Naniwastar, on the other hand, is a comedy capital.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.220
She's a Jokerian! Beep boop blork!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.090
Quit it!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.180
Still, Nagisa, haven't you watched any TV after coming here?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.540
I've been too busy with lessons and whatnot.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.310
The successor members appear on TV now and then.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.490
Nyan~

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.660
We will be broadcasting a regular variety show

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.130
in which you understudies will appear.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.750
What's a "variety show"?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.100
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.960
Oh my gosh. Oh my gosh!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.500
Nagisa!

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.230
Th-This is...

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.760
a variety show?!

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.500
Here I go!

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.500
No way, no way, no way, no way!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.960
Pork fillet over rice!

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.050
No, no, I can't do it!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.300
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.180
No, no, no!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.810
I can't, I can't, I can't!

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.150
Augh, I look so lame!

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:36.940
Excellent reaction technique, Makoto-san.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.770
It wasn't a technique!

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:45.210
They could have started with something easier than bungee jumping.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.160
So do variety shows mostly
involve stuff like this?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.990
No. There are various types of segments.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.830
Sis-sis, lookit me!

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.700
There are funny face face-offs...

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.460
I'm on camera.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.460
This is so embarrassing.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.760
What else is there?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.220
Cooking shows, for one.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:15.200
Um, Mimori-san...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.690
That outfit...

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.850
Don't you think it's a bit re—

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:19.690
Okay!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.380
It's done!

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.070
Boing!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.210
Boing~

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.660
Mimori-san, that's—

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.450
There are talk shows, too.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.820
M-My most treasured possession?

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:39.980
Right, um, it would be this
ribbon my mother made.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:45.530
Uh, my mother is a housewife, and she
married my father after they fell in love...

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.810
How can I just talk without rehearsing at all?

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:53.010
It's impossible.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.160
I didn't get any laughs at all!

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.180
You had excellent facial expression technique, Makoto-san.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.850
I told you, it wasn't a technique!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:06.080
Our concerts and handshake events really didn't prepare us for <i>this.</i>

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.740
I'm glad you girls are with me.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.160
Chieri's probably by herself
at a gravure shoot right now.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.830
Yeah, probably.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.290
B-By herself? Just the thought of it makes me nauseous!

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.470
Chan-Chie, that's enough for today.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.050
I'm fine. I can keep going.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.300
You think so?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.180
I feel like you're not as radiant as usual.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.800
They've been power pushing you lately, haven't they?

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.610
"Perhaps she's got some
big sponsor behind her."

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.150
So the rumors go.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.300
Thank you very much!

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.870
Oh, Chieri!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.150
Ah, good morning.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.090
Are you here for a gravure shoot too, Yuuko-san?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:06.990
Yep!

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.450
Gonna give 'em my sexiest poses!

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:15.350
Chan-Yuu! Hurry up!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.440
Coming!

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.100
Later, rival.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.460
Right.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.470
The experiment failed.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:51.760
It appears we are unable
to achieve that light yet.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.590
Chieri. Cultivate your radiance.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:00.430
Zodiac will appreciate it.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.940
What's wrong?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.720
You look troubled.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.590
I can't stop thinking about it.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.640
Kasumigastar is one of the
government's primary strongholds.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:21.080
Yet we managed to break in and out so easily.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.370
So you think there's more to the story?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.840
I'm not sure.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.970
WOTA intelligence agents
are looking into it right now.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:38.340
Looks like we have to be ready by five tomorrow morning.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.810
TV work is backbreaking.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:43.880
Really?

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.970
I'm enjoying myself.

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:49.280
It's our chance to make the fans remember us!

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:50.900
Chance, chance!

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.710
You two are sure in high spirits.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.540
Our performances and lessons are continuing as usual.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.240
Gotta eat to keep up my stamina.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.380
We have fewer guerrilla concerts, though.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.770
Entertainment suppression has grown harsher,

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.370
and DES attacks have also become fiercer.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.550
It's to be expected.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:17.400
Still, I feel our time could be better spent on concerts than TV shows.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.300
Approach any job the same way!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.260
With a smile and with all your energy!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.980
Takamina-san!

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:27.730
You've never been on TV before, so it might take some adjusting,

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:31.060
but I promise the reward will be worth it!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.590
O-Okay...

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.440
Oh yeah. Nagisa.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:37.650
Yes?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.870
You still haven't made your
poster for the Elections, right?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.350
If you need any help, just come and ask.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:46.950
My door's always open.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:47.750
Later!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:51.700
Okay. Thank you.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.240
The General Elections, huh?

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.030
We'd nearly forgotten about them.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.220
Chieri hasn't done hers yet, either.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:22.360
It's time for the first AKB0048 Impressions Contest!

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:18.320
The first

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:39.010
I'll be doing an impression of Umeda Ayaka-san the 3rd.

00:11:47.110 --> 00:11:49.790
That was my impression of Grumbly snoring!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.170
Quit it!

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:56.800
Um...

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:01.150
This is my impression of Yuuko-san
sleeping while clinging to Sayaka-san.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.540
Chieri-chan!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:09.910
Chieri!

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.150
Whoa.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:11.870
Yeah.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.760
I'm going to do an impression of this Kirara.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.820
That's enough.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:21.720
Stop the cameras.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.650
The recording is cancelled.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:32.320
I haven't said a word since
the start of recording, but...

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.940
this is a travesty!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.620
But just shoving us in front of the cameras—

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:42.910
Are you saying you're helpless unless we hold your hands?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.620
I don't plan to shirk our TV work.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.480
Chieri...

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:53.980
I agree that we're not meeting expectations.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.080
However, I would rather be doing concerts.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.460
I second that.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:04.710
The entertainment crackdown gives
us even more reason to hold concerts.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.800
Sis-sis...

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:15.170
I want you to carefully reflect on
the purpose of what you're doing.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:22.780
We can't do anything.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:22.980
...dekinai

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.480
We can't do it yet.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.480
sugu ni dekinai

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.480
But that just means we're full of potential.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.480
dakara bokura ni kanousei ga aru nda

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.030
The rain has passed.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.030
ame wa yanda

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.490
The wind has died.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.490
kaze wa yanda

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.780
A brand new light

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.780
mita koto no nai

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.490
is shining down.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.490
hikari ga sasu yo

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.910
Now is the time.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.910
ima ga toki da

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:40.410
You've been reborn, Beginner!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:40.410
kimi wa umarekawatta Beginner!

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:48.520
Nagisa.

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.700
I haven't seen you dance in a while.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:53.820
It's really something!

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:57.900
You're always most radiant when you're singing and dancing.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.190
Oh, sorry!

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:03.810
I didn't mean you're not good at other stuff.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.910
It's just... a feeling.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.220
I can't concentrate on my work.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:12.750
Huh?

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:16.140
I'm worried that this attention
is because of the trial.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:19.320
I'm not sure if I'm popular because of <i>me.</i>

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:21.770
Of course you are!

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.670
Everyone was moved by your words.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.130
You think so?

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.680
Chieri...

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:32.810
I want to show my true skills in concert.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.600
I want to get elected because of my skill.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.360
It's Nagisa and Cherry!

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:41.060
"Cherry"?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:44.190
Are you still up practicing?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.400
Yukirin-san. Kojiharu-san.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:54.890
You're worried that your
popularity is superficial, Cherry?

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:58.370
So that's why you argued with
Tsubasa-san about doing concerts.

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:07.810
Neither of you have finished
your Election posters, have you?

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:09.540
Yeah.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.510
Not yet.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:16.160
Then maybe we should show you <i>that.</i>

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:20.700
Nyan-Nyan couldn't agree more!

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:25.950
What is "that"?

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:29.150
Acchan at the last General Election.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.780
It's a video of Maeda Atsuko-san the 13th.

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:46.310
What's this light?

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:48.590
Thank you, everyone!

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:50.460
Acchan...

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.540
Thank you.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.100
That voice...

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.610
Thank you!

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.310
I knew it was her.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.650
<i>You want to reach them, don't you?</i>

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:01.810
The voice we heard was Acchan the 13th.

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:06.530
Is this... the radiance of a Center Nova?

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:11.900
If I could turn into light and
shine on you all forevermore...

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:15.530
After the elections

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.790
That was so moving!

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.700
I want to be like Acchan someday!

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:20.840
Me too!

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:21.420
Me three!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.640
I wanna be like her!

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.670
Acchan the 13th is my rival!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:31.880
At next year's Elections, I'll definitely,
<i>definitely</i> beat her and become Center Nova!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:31.880
72nd generation understudy

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:31.880
Kimishima Hikari Non-AEPS

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:38.100
If I recall correctly, she succeeded Ooshima Yuuko shortly after this.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:42.420
<i>Even when she was an understudy like us,</i>

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:45.060
<i>she wasn't afraid to challenge the successors.</i>

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.980
72nd generation understudy

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.980
Kimishima Hikari Non-AEPS

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.450
<i>It's clear how determined she was.</i>

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.980
To all my fans, I hope you'll keep supporting me!

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.560
Got it?

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.240
Let's go out there and blow them away!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.500
Blow them way away!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.250
Okay!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.250
What's gotten into Kanata-san?

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:07.610
Suzuko-san did some research
after what happened yesterday.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:13.670
Our show is being broadcast on planets
where the Entertainment Ban is strictest.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:18.640
On those planets, it's hard to hold mass public events like concerts.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:20.000
Meaning...

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.940
They can't attend concerts,

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:27.580
but they might be able to receive TV
broadcasts from WOTA's underground network.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.940
Heart-Pounding

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.950
Dodge Ball

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.740
The losing team has to do a punishment game?

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:40.860
We should have thrown in the towel
when we didn't get on Kanata-san's team.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:43.000
Don't give up just yet!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.000
If we're doing this, we're giving it our all!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:11.650
Nice catch there!

00:18:13.750 --> 00:18:14.900
M-Mimori-san!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:15.490
Your clothes!

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:18.790
Oh dear!

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:23.120
Mimori?!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.100
All right!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.580
I'm back in action!

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:30.010
Her Kirara!

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.200
You're right!

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:31.980
It's so beautiful!

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:32.460
Wow!

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:37.670
<i>This isn't a concert, yet Mimori-san's Kirara is glowing so brightly.</i>

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.630
<i>The audience is having fun too.</i>

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.060
<i>And so am I!</i>

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:43.970
Take this!

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:49.040
sora ni chirabatta hoshi no

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:49.040
I wonder which of the stars in the sky

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:55.090
dore ga ichiban ni kagayaku no darou

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:55.090
glows brightest of them all?

00:18:55.090 --> 00:19:00.970
kikaretemo daremo kitto kotaerarenai

00:18:55.090 --> 00:19:00.970
You can ask anyone, and they won't know,

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.320
Nice one, Orine!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:09.690
kurayami no saki ni koko kara mienai hikari ga aru

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:09.690
but beyond the darkness, a new light awaits us.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:03.020
<i>I get it.</i>

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.870
<i>By being true to our hearts,</i>

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.750
<i>we can sincerely enjoy ourselves now!</i>

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:12.210
Okay, losing team! Punishment game time!

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:15.780
suteeji no katasumi de mogakitsuzukeru

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:15.780
In the corner of the stage, I struggle on.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:17.170
It seems we lacked offensive
capabilities aside from Kanata-san.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:23.950
kuyashisa ya munashisa mo seishun no toki

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:23.950
The pain and disappointment are all a part of my youth.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:17.920
You're so cute!

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:18.780
Kanata-chan!

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.130
Sonata!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:28.060
<i>Whether in concert or elsewhere, what's most important is to act from the heart.</i>

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:29.290
shoujotachi yo mousugu yoake ga kuru

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:29.290
Stand up, girls! The dawn is nearly here.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.020
Sis-sis!

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:34.880
yume no mirai wa kore kara hajimaru

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:34.880
We've barely begun on the road to our dreams.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:41.640
shoujotachi yo nanimo akirameru na

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:41.640
Stand up girls! There's no reason to lose hope.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:40.120
Well aren't you smiling wonderfully today?

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:47.520
kanashii koto nanka subete sutete

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:47.520
Shake yourself free from all your sadness.

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:53.690
zenryoku de zenryoku de

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:53.690
With all our might,

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:57.740
hashiru nda

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:57.740
we'll take off running.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:04.380
<i>I'm still uncertain about the General Elections.</i>

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:03.810
Motomiya Nagisa

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:03.980
Ichijou Yuuka

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:03.980
Kishida Mimori

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:06.150
<i>But...</i>

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.570
Sono Chieri

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:12.570
I'll definitely become
a successor

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.490
77th Gen Motomiya Nagisa

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.210
Thank you!

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:30.450
See you again!

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:36.620
What now?

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.460
A blackout?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.010
Darky-darky!

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:52.100
This is AKB0048's general manager, Katagiri Tsubasa, speaking.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.810
Tsubasa-san?

00:20:55.590 --> 00:21:00.320
Concerning the 0048 SC
New Single General Elections,

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:02.820
the early results are in!

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:06.540
She's announcing them... right here?

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.790
E-Early results?

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:12.040
The Election rankings as of now.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.520
Here we go.

00:21:15.610 --> 00:21:19.080
Ten members will be elected this round.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.010
Therefore, I will start announcing from tenth place.

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:26.220
In tenth place: Kitahara Rie the 9th!

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:26.430
th place

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:26.430
10

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:31.190
Kitahara Rie

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:31.190
The 9th

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.150
In ninth place:

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:39.200
77th generation understudy...

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:41.110
Sono Chieri!

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.070
th place

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:44.070
Sono Chieri

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:44.070
Understudy

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:44.070
7th Gen

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:07.810
Chieri...

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:28.030
The wish from that day

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:28.030
itsuka no negai wa

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:32.740
sleeps in the ground.

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:32.740
tsuchi no naka de nemutte

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:37.120
When the promised time comes,

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:37.120
yakusoku no jikoku ni

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:41.880
it shall sprout a bud of hope.

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:41.880
kibou no me ga deru nda

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:45.800
Back when we first met,

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:45.800
futari ga deatta koro

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:50.890
our dreams were but seeds.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:50.890
yume nado mada tane datta

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:54.810
How long will it take

00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:54.810
dore kurai toki ga sugi

00:22:54.810 --> 00:23:00.400
before they finally bloom?

00:22:54.810 --> 00:23:00.400
hana wa saku no darou

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:05.530
I offer my tears to you.

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:05.530
kono namida wo kimi ni sasagu

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:10.070
If it will help you glow with greater radiance,

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:10.070
motto kimi ga kagayaku nara

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:12.450
then from up here, in this silent sky,

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:12.450
zutto mimamotteta

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:15.540
where I've been watching over you,

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:15.540
chinmoku no sora kara

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:20.120
I shall now fall as rain.

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:20.120
ima boku wa ame ni narou

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:23.630
Ah, I'll offer them to you.

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:23.630
a, kimi ni sasagu

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:28.220
All that I can do right now

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:28.220
konna boku ni dekiru koto wa

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:33.640
is ease the emptiness you feel, if only a little.

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:33.640
kimi no munashisa wo sukoshi demo iyasu koto

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:38.600
And so, I shall fall as rain.

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:38.600
saa boku wa ame ni narou

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:49.490
The time has finally come! Welcome to the 0048 SC General Elections!

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:52.030
Well of course we're all antsy.
It's the General Elections after all.

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.030
The Elections are like a festival.

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:55.910
If you don't enjoy them, you're missing out!

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:59.020
What's the deal with the Elections anyway?

00:23:57.410 --> 00:23:59.990
- The Idols' Dark Before Dawn-
